        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Flushing a tankless water heater is an hour with a pump, a bucket and a few gallons of vinegar, and it is the single maintenance task that decides whether the heater lasts ten years or twenty. Check for isolation valves first, circulate for at least 60 minutes, rinse, clean the inlet screen, and on electric units purge every bit of air before the breakers go back on.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Set the interval by your water hardness, not by habit, and if you find yourself flushing twice a year, fix the water rather than the heater. Buy a flush kit once, put the date on your calendar, and the most expensive failure in the category becomes the easiest one to avoid.
          </p>
